{"id":"50d2194f2a21f1f5f939553d767c5c8884c152a0","url":"https://www.mecharoyale.com/","title":"MECHAROYALE","site_name":"Buzzing","source":"www.mecharoyale.com","byline":null,"excerpt":"BAY SPIN-UP0%","content_html":"<DIV class=\"page\" id=\"readability-page-1\"><div id=\"splash\">\n  <!-- ── Home menu — three full-height columns: the station RAIL on the left\n       (wordmark · one large key per station), the active STATION in the\n       middle, and the steady flight DECK on the right (crew · machine · PLAY).\n       The fullscreen hangar scene (#hangar-bg) — the picked mech, the pilot +\n       crew on their floor rings, the Orbital Station bay — renders behind all\n       of it, with the middle column as its window. ── -->\n  <!-- ── BAY SPIN-UP — what the terminal is doing while the bay powers on ──\n       Lives in the HTML, not built by the bundle, because the wait it narrates\n       STARTS with the bundle: the client is ~600-900 ms of download and parse\n       before a line of our code runs, and a readout that needs that code to\n       exist can only appear after the part it was meant to explain. It paints\n       with the rest of the menu at ~130 ms, already showing its first step.\n       Every line is a REAL signal (see boot-log.ts + main.ts) — nothing here is\n       a timed animation pretending to be progress. -->\n  <div id=\"boot-log\" aria-live=\"polite\" aria-label=\"Bay spin-up status\">\n    <p><span data-i18n=\"spinup.head\">BAY SPIN-UP</span><span>0%</span></p>\n    <ol>\n      <li data-step=\"client\"><b></b><span data-i18n=\"spinup.client\">LOADING CLIENT</span><i></i></li>\n      <li data-step=\"link\"><b></b><span data-i18n=\"spinup.link\">LINK TO COMMAND</span><i></i></li>\n      <li data-step=\"terrain\"><b></b><span data-i18n=\"spinup.terrain\">SURVEYING TERRAIN</span><i></i></li>\n      <li data-step=\"bay\"><b></b><span data-i18n=\"spinup.bay\">POWERING UP BAY</span><i></i></li>\n    </ol>\n    \n  </div>\n\n  \n\n  <!-- The boot handler's entry point (main.ts binds by id). The PLAY button\n       proxies a click here — the whole staged boot sequence stays\n       byte-for-byte the one the old PLAY button ran. -->\n  <div id=\"controls-desktop\">\n    <p data-i18n-html=\"controls.desktopLine1\"><b>WASD</b> Move &#160;·&#160; <b>Mouse</b> Look &#160;·&#160; <b>Click</b> Attack &#160;·&#160; <b>E</b> Interact &#160;·&#160; <b>Q</b> Swap weapon</p>\n    <p data-i18n-html=\"controls.desktopLine2\"><b>I</b> Inventory &#160;·&#160; <b>M</b> Map &#160;·&#160; <b>SPACE</b> Jump/Swim &#160;·&#160; <b>CTRL</b> Dive &#160;·&#160; <b>Enter</b> Chat &#160;·&#160; <b>ESC</b> Settings &#160;·&#160; <b>C</b> Camera</p>\n  </div>\n  \n  \n  </div><div id=\"settings-panel\">\n    <h2 data-i18n=\"settings.title\">SETTINGS</h2>\n\n    <!-- Tab strip: switches which .settings-tab-panel below is visible. Every\n         control keeps its original id, so settings.ts / keybinds.ts wiring is\n         unaffected — tabs are pure presentation (see setupTabs in settings.ts). -->\n    \n\n    <!-- ── GAMEPLAY ──────────────────────────────────────────────── -->\n    <div data-tab-panel=\"gameplay\">\n      <p>LANGUAGE</p>\n      <p><label data-i18n=\"settings.languageLabel\">Language</label><span id=\"set-language-host\"></span></p>\n\n      <p>GAMEPLAY</p>\n      <!-- (The Auto-Heal row left with the pilot heal/potion layer, ticket\n           c4d11dd2 — kept removed through the ticket-3564384e merge.) -->\n      <!-- The CAPTAIN'S crew-weapon policy (ticket 3564384e): designate &\n           lock — the head-of-line queue rule, the DEFAULT (one weapon, one\n           aim: the drawn arm can only follow one person's look) — or free\n           fire, anybody who has selected a socket may pull its trigger,\n           several at once. A per-player preference; it is spoken to whichever\n           hull this player CAPTAINS (mech-weapons setCrewWeaponPreference),\n           where the server re-gates it and broadcasts it to the whole\n           bridge. -->\n      <p><label data-i18n=\"settings.crewWeapons\">Crew weapons (captain)</label>\n        \n      </p>\n\n      <p>TUTORIAL</p>\n      <p><label data-i18n=\"settings.resetTutorial\">Reset tutorial progress</label></p>\n    </div>\n\n    <!-- ── AUDIO ─────────────────────────────────────────────────── -->\n    <div data-tab-panel=\"audio\">\n      <p>AUDIO</p>\n      <p><label data-i18n=\"settings.masterVolume\">Master Volume</label><span id=\"vol-master-val\">50</span></p>\n      <p><label data-i18n=\"settings.sfxVolume\">SFX Volume</label><span id=\"vol-sfx-val\">70</span></p>\n      <p><label data-i18n=\"settings.musicVolume\">Music Volume</label><span id=\"vol-music-val\">30</span></p>\n      <p><label data-i18n=\"settings.ambientVolume\">Ambient Volume</label><span id=\"vol-ambient-val\">40</span></p>\n\n      <p>VOICE CHAT</p>\n      <p><label data-i18n=\"settings.voiceMode\">Microphone</label>\n        \n      </p>\n      <p><label data-i18n=\"settings.voiceVolume\">Voice Volume</label><span id=\"vol-voice-val\">80</span></p>\n    </div>\n\n    <!-- ── GRAPHICS ──────────────────────────────────────────────── -->\n    <div data-tab-panel=\"graphics\">\n      <p>VIDEO</p>\n      <div><p><label data-i18n=\"settings.graphicsQuality\">Graphics Quality</label></p><!-- One-shot levels: picking one applies (and persists) the whole\n             bundle below it. \"Custom\" is DISPLAY-ONLY — the panel selects it\n             once an individual control no longer matches the chosen level;\n             picking it changes nothing. There is no adaptive option: nothing\n             in a running session moves a graphics setting (ticket 75e20c80). -->\n        </div>\n      <!-- Graphics API. Auto is WebGPU wherever the browser has it and WebGL 2\n           otherwise (render-backend.ts decides before the renderer is built);\n           WebGL 2 pins the compatibility path. A change RELOADS — a backend\n           cannot be swapped under a live renderer. Menu-safe (settings.ts\n           setupRenderBackendSelect): a player whose bay is black has to be able\n           to reach this before pressing PLAY. The readout under it is the\n           backend actually running, for support conversations. -->\n      <p><label data-i18n=\"settings.renderBackend\">Graphics API</label>\n        \n      </p>\n      <p><label data-i18n=\"settings.renderBackendActive\">Active renderer</label>\n        <span id=\"set-render-backend-active\">—</span>\n      </p>\n      <p><label data-i18n=\"settings.renderScale\">Render Scale</label>\n        \n      </p>\n      <p><label data-i18n=\"settings.drawDistance\">Draw Distance</label>\n        \n        <datalist id=\"draw-distance-notches\">\n          <option value=\"0\"></option><option value=\"1\"></option><option value=\"2\"></option>\n          <option value=\"3\"></option><option value=\"4\"></option><option value=\"5\"></option>\n          <option value=\"6\"></option>\n        </datalist>\n        <span id=\"set-draw-distance-val\">Extreme</span>\n      </p>\n      <p><label data-i18n=\"settings.shadows\">Shadows</label>\n        \n      </p>\n      <p><label data-i18n=\"settings.surfaces\">Surface Detail</label>\n        \n      </p>\n      <p><label data-i18n=\"settings.atmosphere\">Atmosphere</label>\n        \n      </p>\n      <p><label data-i18n=\"settings.effects\">Effects</label>\n        \n      </p>\n      <p><label data-i18n=\"settings.groundDetail\">Ground Detail</label>\n        \n      </p>\n      <p><label data-i18n=\"settings.vegetation\">Vegetation</label>\n        \n      </p>\n      <p><label data-i18n=\"settings.groundTexture\">Ground Texture</label>\n        \n      </p>\n      <p><label data-i18n=\"settings.textureTiling\">Texture Tiling (m)</label><span id=\"set-texture-repeat-val\">12</span></p>\n      <p><label data-i18n=\"settings.fov\">FOV</label><span id=\"set-fov-val\">70</span></p>\n    </div>\n\n    <!-- ── CONTROLS ──────────────────────────────────────────────── -->\n    <div data-tab-panel=\"controls\">\n      <p>CONTROLS</p>\n      <p><label data-i18n=\"settings.controlScheme\">Control Scheme</label>\n        \n      </p>\n      <!-- Robot camera mode (cockpit ↔ third-person boom); on foot the view\n           is always first person. State + persistence live in chase-camera.ts\n           (own localStorage key, shared with the C key and the mobile 📷\n           button) — settings.ts wires this select outside the\n           SettingsCallbacks blob. -->\n      <p><label data-i18n=\"settings.cameraMode\">Robot camera</label>\n        \n      </p>\n      <p><label data-i18n=\"settings.mouseSensitivity\">Mouse Sensitivity</label><span id=\"set-sens-val\">4</span></p>\n      <!-- How the machine's REAL aim is shown against the crosshair\n           (client/mech-aim-reticle-hud): the crosshair opening with the\n           inaccuracy (default), a faded second cross where the guns really\n           point, or both. Persisted under its own key by settings.ts. -->\n      <p><label data-i18n=\"settings.aimReticle\">Aim reticle</label>\n        \n      </p>\n\n      <p>HOTBAR KEYS</p>\n      <!-- Per-slot rebind rows are built by keybinds.ts (labels interpolate the\n           slot number, which static data-i18n markup can't). -->\n      \n      <p><label data-i18n=\"settings.resetKeybinds\">Reset key bindings</label></p>\n    </div>\n\n    <p>[ CLOSE ]</p>\n  </div></DIV>","content_text":"BAY SPIN-UP0% LOADING CLIENT LINK TO COMMAND SURVEYING TERRAIN POWERING UP BAY WASD Move · Mouse Look · Click Attack · E Interact · Q Swap weapon I Inventory · M Map · SPACE Jump/Swim · CTRL Dive · Enter Chat · ESC Settings · C Camera SETTINGS LANGUAGE Language GAMEPLAY Crew weapons (captain) TUTORIAL Reset tutorial progress AUDIO Master Volume50 SFX Volume70 Music Volume30 Ambient Volume40 VOICE CHAT Microphone Voice Volume80 VIDEO Graphics Quality Graphics API Active renderer — Render Scale Draw Distance Extreme Shadows Surface Detail Atmosphere Effects Ground Detail Vegetation Ground Texture Texture Tiling (m)12 FOV70 CONTROLS Control Scheme Robot camera Mouse Sensitivity4 Aim reticle HOTBAR KEYS Reset key bindings [ CLOSE ]","fetched_at":"2026-09-14T16:09:37.940Z","ok":true,"blocks":[{"html_en":"<p><span data-i18n=\"spinup.head\">BAY SPIN-UP</span><span>0%</span></p>","sentences":[{"en":"BAY SPIN-UP0%","zh":null}]},{"html_en":"<li data-step=\"client\"><b></b><span data-i18n=\"spinup.client\">LOADING CLIENT</span><i></i></li>","sentences":[{"en":"LOADING CLIENT","zh":null}]},{"html_en":"<li data-step=\"link\"><b></b><span data-i18n=\"spinup.link\">LINK TO COMMAND</span><i></i></li>","sentences":[{"en":"LINK TO COMMAND","zh":null}]},{"html_en":"<li data-step=\"terrain\"><b></b><span data-i18n=\"spinup.terrain\">SURVEYING TERRAIN</span><i></i></li>","sentences":[{"en":"SURVEYING TERRAIN","zh":null}]},{"html_en":"<li data-step=\"bay\"><b></b><span data-i18n=\"spinup.bay\">POWERING UP BAY</span><i></i></li>","sentences":[{"en":"POWERING UP BAY","zh":null}]},{"html_en":"<p data-i18n-html=\"controls.desktopLine1\"><b>WASD</b> Move &#160;·&#160; <b>Mouse</b> Look &#160;·&#160; <b>Click</b> Attack &#160;·&#160; <b>E</b> Interact &#160;·&#160; <b>Q</b> Swap weapon</p>","sentences":[{"en":"WASD Move · Mouse Look · Click Attack · E Interact · Q Swap weapon","zh":null}]},{"html_en":"<p data-i18n-html=\"controls.desktopLine2\"><b>I</b> Inventory &#160;·&#160; <b>M</b> Map &#160;·&#160; <b>SPACE</b> Jump/Swim &#160;·&#160; <b>CTRL</b> Dive &#160;·&#160; <b>Enter</b> Chat &#160;·&#160; <b>ESC</b> Settings &#160;·&#160; <b>C</b> Camera</p>","sentences":[{"en":"I Inventory · M Map · SPACE Jump/Swim · CTRL Dive · Enter Chat · ESC Settings · C Camera","zh":null}]},{"html_en":"<h2 data-i18n=\"settings.title\">SETTINGS</h2>","sentences":[{"en":"SETTINGS","zh":null}]},{"html_en":"<p>LANGUAGE</p>","sentences":[{"en":"LANGUAGE","zh":null}]},{"html_en":"<p><label data-i18n=\"settings.languageLabel\">Language</label><span id=\"set-language-host\"></span></p>","sentences":[{"en":"Language","zh":"语言"}]},{"html_en":"<p>GAMEPLAY</p>","sentences":[{"en":"GAMEPLAY","zh":null}]},{"html_en":"<p><label data-i18n=\"settings.crewWeapons\">Crew weapons (captain)</label>\n        \n      </p>","sentences":[{"en":"Crew weapons (captain)","zh":null}]},{"html_en":"<p>TUTORIAL</p>","sentences":[{"en":"TUTORIAL","zh":null}]},{"html_en":"<p><label data-i18n=\"settings.resetTutorial\">Reset tutorial progress</label></p>","sentences":[{"en":"Reset tutorial progress","zh":null}]},{"html_en":"<p>AUDIO</p>","sentences":[]},{"html_en":"<p><label data-i18n=\"settings.masterVolume\">Master Volume</label><span id=\"vol-master-val\">50</span></p>","sentences":[{"en":"Master Volume50","zh":null}]},{"html_en":"<p><label data-i18n=\"settings.sfxVolume\">SFX Volume</label><span id=\"vol-sfx-val\">70</span></p>","sentences":[{"en":"SFX Volume70","zh":null}]},{"html_en":"<p><label data-i18n=\"settings.musicVolume\">Music Volume</label><span id=\"vol-music-val\">30</span></p>","sentences":[{"en":"Music Volume30","zh":null}]},{"html_en":"<p><label data-i18n=\"settings.ambientVolume\">Ambient Volume</label><span id=\"vol-ambient-val\">40</span></p>","sentences":[{"en":"Ambient Volume40","zh":null}]},{"html_en":"<p>VOICE CHAT</p>","sentences":[{"en":"VOICE CHAT","zh":null}]},{"html_en":"<p><label data-i18n=\"settings.voiceMode\">Microphone</label>\n        \n      </p>","sentences":[{"en":"Microphone","zh":"麦克风"}]},{"html_en":"<p><label data-i18n=\"settings.voiceVolume\">Voice Volume</label><span id=\"vol-voice-val\">80</span></p>","sentences":[{"en":"Voice Volume80","zh":null}]},{"html_en":"<p>VIDEO</p>","sentences":[]},{"html_en":"<p><label data-i18n=\"settings.graphicsQuality\">Graphics Quality</label></p>","sentences":[{"en":"Graphics Quality","zh":null}]},{"html_en":"<p><label data-i18n=\"settings.renderBackend\">Graphics API</label>\n        \n      </p>","sentences":[{"en":"Graphics API","zh":"图形API"}]},{"html_en":"<p><label data-i18n=\"settings.renderBackendActive\">Active renderer</label>\n        <span id=\"set-render-backend-active\">—</span>\n      </p>","sentences":[{"en":"Active renderer —","zh":null}]},{"html_en":"<p><label data-i18n=\"settings.renderScale\">Render Scale</label>\n        \n      </p>","sentences":[{"en":"Render Scale","zh":null}]},{"html_en":"<p><label data-i18n=\"settings.drawDistance\">Draw Distance</label>\n        \n        <datalist id=\"draw-distance-notches\">\n          <option value=\"0\"></option><option value=\"1\"></option><option value=\"2\"></option>\n          <option value=\"3\"></option><option value=\"4\"></option><option value=\"5\"></option>\n          <option value=\"6\"></option>\n        </datalist>\n        <span id=\"set-draw-distance-val\">Extreme</span>\n      </p>","sentences":[{"en":"Draw Distance Extreme","zh":null}]},{"html_en":"<p><label data-i18n=\"settings.shadows\">Shadows</label>\n        \n      </p>","sentences":[{"en":"Shadows","zh":null}]},{"html_en":"<p><label data-i18n=\"settings.surfaces\">Surface Detail</label>\n        \n      </p>","sentences":[{"en":"Surface Detail","zh":null}]},{"html_en":"<p><label data-i18n=\"settings.atmosphere\">Atmosphere</label>\n        \n      </p>","sentences":[{"en":"Atmosphere","zh":null}]},{"html_en":"<p><label data-i18n=\"settings.effects\">Effects</label>\n        \n      </p>","sentences":[{"en":"Effects","zh":"效果"}]},{"html_en":"<p><label data-i18n=\"settings.groundDetail\">Ground Detail</label>\n        \n      </p>","sentences":[{"en":"Ground Detail","zh":null}]},{"html_en":"<p><label data-i18n=\"settings.vegetation\">Vegetation</label>\n        \n      </p>","sentences":[{"en":"Vegetation","zh":"植被"}]},{"html_en":"<p><label data-i18n=\"settings.groundTexture\">Ground Texture</label>\n        \n      </p>","sentences":[{"en":"Ground Texture","zh":null}]},{"html_en":"<p><label data-i18n=\"settings.textureTiling\">Texture Tiling (m)</label><span id=\"set-texture-repeat-val\">12</span></p>","sentences":[{"en":"Texture Tiling (m)12","zh":null}]},{"html_en":"<p><label data-i18n=\"settings.fov\">FOV</label><span id=\"set-fov-val\">70</span></p>","sentences":[]},{"html_en":"<p>CONTROLS</p>","sentences":[{"en":"CONTROLS","zh":null}]},{"html_en":"<p><label data-i18n=\"settings.controlScheme\">Control Scheme</label>\n        \n      </p>","sentences":[{"en":"Control Scheme","zh":null}]},{"html_en":"<p><label data-i18n=\"settings.cameraMode\">Robot camera</label>\n        \n      </p>","sentences":[{"en":"Robot camera","zh":null}]},{"html_en":"<p><label data-i18n=\"settings.mouseSensitivity\">Mouse Sensitivity</label><span id=\"set-sens-val\">4</span></p>","sentences":[{"en":"Mouse Sensitivity4","zh":null}]},{"html_en":"<p><label data-i18n=\"settings.aimReticle\">Aim reticle</label>\n        \n      </p>","sentences":[{"en":"Aim reticle","zh":null}]},{"html_en":"<p>HOTBAR KEYS</p>","sentences":[{"en":"HOTBAR KEYS","zh":null}]},{"html_en":"<p><label data-i18n=\"settings.resetKeybinds\">Reset key bindings</label></p>","sentences":[{"en":"Reset key bindings","zh":null}]},{"html_en":"<p>[ CLOSE ]</p>","sentences":[]}],"translated":true,"content_html_zh":"<div class=\"page\" id=\"readability-page-1\"><div id=\"splash\">\n  <!-- ── Home menu — three full-height columns: the station RAIL on the left\n       (wordmark · one large key per station), the active STATION in the\n       middle, and the steady flight DECK on the right (crew · machine · PLAY).\n       The fullscreen hangar scene (#hangar-bg) — the picked mech, the pilot +\n       crew on their floor rings, the Orbital Station bay — renders behind all\n       of it, with the middle column as its window. ── -->\n  <!-- ── BAY SPIN-UP — what the terminal is doing while the bay powers on ──\n       Lives in the HTML, not built by the bundle, because the wait it narrates\n       STARTS with the bundle: the client is ~600-900 ms of download and parse\n       before a line of our code runs, and a readout that needs that code to\n       exist can only appear after the part it was meant to explain. It paints\n       with the rest of the menu at ~130 ms, already showing its first step.\n       Every line is a REAL signal (see boot-log.ts + main.ts) — nothing here is\n       a timed animation pretending to be progress. -->\n  <div id=\"boot-log\" aria-live=\"polite\" aria-label=\"Bay spin-up status\">\n    <p>BAY SPIN-UP0%</p>\n    <ol>\n      <li data-step=\"client\">LOADING CLIENT</li>\n      <li data-step=\"link\">LINK TO COMMAND</li>\n      <li data-step=\"terrain\">SURVEYING TERRAIN</li>\n      <li data-step=\"bay\">POWERING UP BAY</li>\n    </ol>\n    \n  </div>\n\n  \n\n  <!-- The boot handler's entry point (main.ts binds by id). The PLAY button\n       proxies a click here — the whole staged boot sequence stays\n       byte-for-byte the one the old PLAY button ran. -->\n  <div id=\"controls-desktop\">\n    <p data-i18n-html=\"controls.desktopLine1\">WASD Move · Mouse Look · Click Attack · E Interact · Q Swap weapon</p>\n    <p data-i18n-html=\"controls.desktopLine2\">I Inventory · M Map · SPACE Jump/Swim · CTRL Dive · Enter Chat · ESC Settings · C Camera</p>\n  </div>\n  \n  \n  </div><div id=\"settings-panel\">\n    <h2 data-i18n=\"settings.title\">SETTINGS</h2>\n\n    <!-- Tab strip: switches which .settings-tab-panel below is visible. Every\n         control keeps its original id, so settings.ts / keybinds.ts wiring is\n         unaffected — tabs are pure presentation (see setupTabs in settings.ts). -->\n    \n\n    <!-- ── GAMEPLAY ──────────────────────────────────────────────── -->\n    <div data-tab-panel=\"gameplay\">\n      <p>LANGUAGE</p>\n      <p>语言</p>\n\n      <p>GAMEPLAY</p>\n      <!-- (The Auto-Heal row left with the pilot heal/potion layer, ticket\n           c4d11dd2 — kept removed through the ticket-3564384e merge.) -->\n      <!-- The CAPTAIN'S crew-weapon policy (ticket 3564384e): designate &\n           lock — the head-of-line queue rule, the DEFAULT (one weapon, one\n           aim: the drawn arm can only follow one person's look) — or free\n           fire, anybody who has selected a socket may pull its trigger,\n           several at once. A per-player preference; it is spoken to whichever\n           hull this player CAPTAINS (mech-weapons setCrewWeaponPreference),\n           where the server re-gates it and broadcasts it to the whole\n           bridge. -->\n      <p>Crew weapons (captain)</p>\n\n      <p>TUTORIAL</p>\n      <p>Reset tutorial progress</p>\n    </div>\n\n    <!-- ── AUDIO ─────────────────────────────────────────────────── -->\n    <div data-tab-panel=\"audio\">\n      <p>AUDIO</p>\n      <p>Master Volume50</p>\n      <p>SFX Volume70</p>\n      <p>Music Volume30</p>\n      <p>Ambient Volume40</p>\n\n      <p>VOICE CHAT</p>\n      <p>麦克风</p>\n      <p>Voice Volume80</p>\n    </div>\n\n    <!-- ── GRAPHICS ──────────────────────────────────────────────── -->\n    <div data-tab-panel=\"graphics\">\n      <p>VIDEO</p>\n      <div><p>Graphics Quality</p><!-- One-shot levels: picking one applies (and persists) the whole\n             bundle below it. \"Custom\" is DISPLAY-ONLY — the panel selects it\n             once an individual control no longer matches the chosen level;\n             picking it changes nothing. There is no adaptive option: nothing\n             in a running session moves a graphics setting (ticket 75e20c80). -->\n        </div>\n      <!-- Graphics API. Auto is WebGPU wherever the browser has it and WebGL 2\n           otherwise (render-backend.ts decides before the renderer is built);\n           WebGL 2 pins the compatibility path. A change RELOADS — a backend\n           cannot be swapped under a live renderer. Menu-safe (settings.ts\n           setupRenderBackendSelect): a player whose bay is black has to be able\n           to reach this before pressing PLAY. The readout under it is the\n           backend actually running, for support conversations. -->\n      <p>图形API</p>\n      <p>Active renderer —</p>\n      <p>Render Scale</p>\n      <p>Draw Distance Extreme</p>\n      <p>Shadows</p>\n      <p>Surface Detail</p>\n      <p>Atmosphere</p>\n      <p>效果</p>\n      <p>Ground Detail</p>\n      <p>植被</p>\n      <p>Ground Texture</p>\n      <p>Texture Tiling (m)12</p>\n      <p><label data-i18n=\"settings.fov\">FOV</label><span id=\"set-fov-val\">70</span></p>\n    </div>\n\n    <!-- ── CONTROLS ──────────────────────────────────────────────── -->\n    <div data-tab-panel=\"controls\">\n      <p>CONTROLS</p>\n      <p>Control Scheme</p>\n      <!-- Robot camera mode (cockpit ↔ third-person boom); on foot the view\n           is always first person. State + persistence live in chase-camera.ts\n           (own localStorage key, shared with the C key and the mobile 📷\n           button) — settings.ts wires this select outside the\n           SettingsCallbacks blob. -->\n      <p>Robot camera</p>\n      <p>Mouse Sensitivity4</p>\n      <!-- How the machine's REAL aim is shown against the crosshair\n           (client/mech-aim-reticle-hud): the crosshair opening with the\n           inaccuracy (default), a faded second cross where the guns really\n           point, or both. Persisted under its own key by settings.ts. -->\n      <p>Aim reticle</p>\n\n      <p>HOTBAR KEYS</p>\n      <!-- Per-slot rebind rows are built by keybinds.ts (labels interpolate the\n           slot number, which static data-i18n markup can't). -->\n      \n      <p>Reset key bindings</p>\n    </div>\n\n    <p>[ CLOSE ]</p>\n  </div></div>"}